  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Varan bhaat is two elements: "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "varan ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "varan"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", a simple cooked dal, and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "bhaat ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "bhaat"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", plain steamed rice. At the table, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "toop",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "toop"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is stirred through. The dal should be very soft and thin. It is poured rather than spooned."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The strength of this dish is in restraint. Do not add extra spices or garnishes beyond turmeric, salt, and ghee. The plain version is the point."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "yellow-split-peas",
              "amount": 200,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "rinsed well",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "basmati-rice",
              "amount": 300,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "rinsed",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "ghee",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "turmeric",
              "amount": 0.5,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "sea-salt-fine",
              "amount": 1.5,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": "divided",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ],
          "defaultServings": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Put yellow split peas in a saucepan with 800ml water and turmeric. Bring to a boil, skim any foam, reduce heat and simmer for 25-30 minutes until very soft and beginning to dissolve."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Season the dal with 1 tsp salt. The dal should be quite thin and pourable. Add more water if it is thick."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Meanwhile, cook basmati rice. Rinse until water runs clear. Add to a pan with 500ml water and 0.5 tsp salt. Bring to a boil, cover, and cook on very low heat for 12 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove rice from heat. Leave covered for 5 minutes to finish steaming."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Serve rice in bowls. Pour hot dal over the top. Add a generous spoonful of ghee to each bowl."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Dal is thick and heavy rather than pourable",
              "cause": "Too little water or cooked on too high a heat",
              "fix": "Add hot water and stir. The varan should have a consistency close to thin soup when hot."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Rice is stodgy and clumped together",
              "cause": "Too much water or lid removed too early",
              "fix": "Use the absorption method: 500ml water to 300g rice. Do not lift the lid during cooking. Leave to rest before fluffing."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Varan bhaat is eaten at every Maharashtrian table, from rural villages to city apartments. It is the meal that Maharashtrian children grow up eating, often with a pickle and a pappad on the side. It appears on the thali at major festivals including Ganesh Chaturthi and Diwali. The combination of plain toor dal, rice, and ghee represents the baseline of Maharashtrian cooking before any other dishes are added."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}